==============================================================================
LEAKAGE CAVEAT — read before treating 'embedding vs cbf' as a clean A/B
==============================================================================
embedding: leave-out user vectors, rebuilt fresh per split, no cross-review
  training step.
cbf: user vectors are a weighted average of each training business's LDA
  topic vector -- also leave-out at the user level -- BUT the underlying
  LDA topic model was trained once on the full corpus back in notebook 02
  and never saved, so it could not be retrained per-split here (out of
  scope). That gives cbf's topic vectors a mild, structural, hard-to-
  quantify advantage that embedding does not share. If embedding matches
  or beats cbf despite this, that's a stronger result than the raw
  numbers show.

